  "title": "B4: promotion.FEATURES planner_routing, baseline Planner metrics, pool.toml [planner.routing] documented defaults and planner_shadow budget (P14, P18, P20)",
  "spec": "Why: promotion.FEATURES (orchestrator/promotion.py:10-25) has no planner_routing entry and collect() no evidence source for it; baseline._metrics (orchestrator/baseline.py:95-121) carries no Planner metrics, so the Fable-only baseline the brief (P20) requires cannot be saved or compared; pool.toml has no [planner.routing] table and no planner_shadow budget although planner_router.load_cfg and planner_shadow read them.\nWhat:\n- promotion.py: FEATURES[\"planner_routing\"] = {\"table\": \"planner.routing\", \"key\": \"mode\", \"modes\": (\"off\", \"shadow\", \"active\"), \"default\": \"shadow\", \"evidence\": \"planner_routing\"}. collect(\"planner_routing\", root): rows = planner_telemetry.read_invocations(root) (guard ImportError -> {\"n\": 0}); n = number of rows with tier == default tier alias \"opus\" (plus shadow rows from planner_shadow.summary(root)[\"n\"] reported as shadow_n); aggregate class_evidence over every distinct (decision_type, band, task_class, architectural) class present in opus rows via planner_scorecard.class_evidence(model=<[models].opus id>, ..., root=root, cfg=cfg): classes_noninferior, classes_inferior, classes_insufficient counts; first_pass_rate and fix_rounds/gate/review deltas averaged over classes with evidence; shadow_agreement_rate from planner_shadow.summary. evaluate() keeps its existing rules; a planner_routing recommendation of promote requires classes_inferior == 0 and classes_noninferior >= 1 in addition (never on token savings). report() includes the new feature automatically.\n- baseline.py: PRIMARY gains (\"fable_tokens_per_accepted_goal\", \"planner_tokens_per_accepted_goal\", \"fable_calls_per_accepted_goal\", \"planner_tokens_per_material_decision\", \"fable_share\") sourced from planner_telemetry.accepted_goal_summary(root) inside _metrics (guard ImportError/Exception -> None values); these are lower-better PRIMARY metrics and never enter NON_INFERIORITY; compare() reports them like the other PRIMARY metrics; save() stores them under metrics. Existing baseline files without those keys compare as None (no crash).\n- pool.toml: add a documented [planner.routing] table with every key at its default and a comment per key (mode = \"shadow\" # off = today's Fable-only behaviour; default_tier = \"opus\"; escalation_tier = \"fable\"; hard_complexity_min = 9; hard_security = true; hard_spec_review_request_changes_min = 2; hard_ambiguous = true; min_samples = 20; shadow_sample_rate = 1.0; fable_reserve_share = 0.2; jev_mode = \"shadow\"; soft_threshold = 0.5) placed after [planner.routes]; add planner_shadow = 1.5 to [limits].max_budget_usd. Comments name the consumer module per key (planner_router.load_cfg docstring table). No other pool.toml change.\n- Tests: tests/test_promotion.py and tests/test_baseline.py extended (existing test names unchanged).",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_promotion.py::test_planner_routing_feature_registered_and_collected \u2014 FEATURES has planner_routing with default shadow; collect under a sandbox root with opus and fable invocation rows returns n, classes_noninferior/inferior/insufficient and shadow_agreement_rate; with no rows returns n 0 without raising",
    "tests/test_promotion.py::test_planner_routing_never_promotes_on_tokens_alone \u2014 evidence with huge token savings but classes_insufficient only yields stay; one inferior class yields stay or demote, never promote; one noninferior class and zero inferior yields promote",
    "tests/test_baseline.py::test_planner_metrics_in_baseline_and_compare \u2014 save under a sandbox root records fable_tokens_per_accepted_goal, planner_tokens_per_accepted_goal, fable_calls_per_accepted_goal, planner_tokens_per_material_decision and fable_share; compare between a baseline lacking them and one having them reports before None without raising and never lists them among non-inferiority flags",
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_planner_routing_table_documented_defaults \u2014 pool.toml parses with tomllib; [planner.routing] holds exactly the twelve documented keys at planner_router._DEFAULTS values and [limits].max_budget_usd.planner_shadow == 1.5; planner_router.load_cfg(cfg) issues no notify"
  ],
